## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of module composition, workspace-based state, and simple CI gates in a beginner-friendly way. It ensures the candidate can wire a wrapper for consistent tagging across environments and validate constraints early in CI.

## Key Concepts

- Terraform modules and wrappers
- Variable validation for environment constraints
- Workspaces and workspace-aware backends
- Per-env state isolation with a single backend
- GitHub Actions gates around terraform plan

## Code Example

```javascript
// modules/env-wrapper/variables.tf
variable "environment" {
  type = string
  description = "Environment name (dev, prod)"
  validation {
    condition = contains(["dev","prod"], var.environment)
    error_message = "environment must be 'dev' or 'prod'"
  }
}
variable "cost_center" {
  type = string
}
```

```javascript
// modules/env-wrapper/main.tf
locals {
  common_tags = {
    Environment = var.environment
    CostCenter  = var.cost_center
  }
}
```
